            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> 1. Improved Word Diff\r\n\r\nThis look a bit too much. Both because it implies extra actions/mappings and a separate `apply_word_hunk` method for the source (which is not trivial because most VCS work on per line basis).\r\n\r\n> 2. Line Range Diff Computation\r\n\r\nThis might be doable in a concise manner, but not sure about when/how to make it usable. I'll think about that. If you can provide a more complete example of how you envision to work with \"partial `set_ref_text()`\", it'll greatly help.",
