            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Here is a use case for \"partial `set_ref_text`\":\r\n\r\nSuppose I'm using an AI plugin like `codecompanion` or `avante` to leverage LLM code generation capabilities. I select a function with a visual selection (e.g., to add documentation to that function) and ask the LLM to generate improvements. The response is saved in a new buffer.\r\n\r\nNow I have:\r\n- The **position** of the original function in the original buffer (e.g., a range of lines).\r\n- A new buffer containing **only** the improved version of the function.\r\n\r\nI want to use mini.diff to compare the differences between the old function and the improved version, but limit the comparison to **only** the lines where the old function is defined, and the text of the new function. Currently, as I understand, mini.diff can only compare the **entire** buffer where the old function resides, rather than restricting it to the relevant lines.",
