        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I want to use mini.diff to compare the differences between the old function and the improved version, but limit the comparison to **only** the lines where the old function is defined, and the text of the new function. Currently, as I understand, mini.diff can only compare the **entire** buffer where the old function resides, rather than restricting it to the relevant lines.\r\n\r\nI would expect here that `set_ref_text()` is called inside a new buffer (which contains **only** the improved version of the function). And reference text is the original content of a function, i.e. lines extracted from the available range of lines in the original buffer. Does this make sense?",
